#!/usr/bin/env bash
# pre-push — the kit's delivery gate: client-identifier guard, live-doctrine citation gate, CI lints of the
# changed files, changelog gate and the continuity + retro gate (build-n4-module campaign PR2). This file is the git hook and a launcher
# only: every allow/refuse decision and every message is in the Go command it runs.
#
# Implementation: go/internal/prepush (go/cmd/pre-push), built on demand by go/go-tool.sh `go_tool_bin`,
# as the toolbelt wrappers are: go/bin/pre-push is rebuilt when it is missing or older than a Go source of
# THIS checkout, so each worktree runs the gate of the tree it pushes from. Needs `go` on PATH to build.
#
# git IS allowed here: a git hook is not a toolbelt/*.sh, so the kit-links.bats L2 rule
# ("no toolbelt script invokes git") does not apply. The Go command owns the git half of the gate (the pushed
# range, its changed paths and its commit messages) and runs the content half from the pushed work tree:
# <toplevel>/build-n4-module-kit/toolbelt/kit-state.sh, sweep-build-state.sh and kit-cite-resolve.sh.
#
# Opt-in: enable with `scripts/install-hooks.sh` (core.hooksPath .githooks). The contract, in order:
#   1. Client-identifier guard, before every other check: niagara-go `client-guard` gets the hook arguments
#      and the whole stdin. Without it on PATH the push goes on only when this machine has no client denylist.
#   2. Every ref line of stdin is gated; the first ref that fails stops the push with its status, after one
#      line naming the refused local -> remote ref. A deleted ref pushes nothing; a new remote branch is
#      gated since it left origin/main (else origin/HEAD), and refused when that base cannot be found.
#   3. Live-doctrine citation gate: a range that changes a live card (go/internal/prepush/paths.go) or
#      the resolver runs `kit-cite-resolve --strict` on the pushed live set. Findings (exit 1) or any tool
#      failure refuse; only exit 3 naming an absent research/modules/clients/memory root skips, with a named
#      stderr line. It is local-only: GitHub runners hold none of those roots, so ci.yml cannot run it.
#   4. CI lints of the changed files: scripts/ci-local.sh --changed --range <pushed range> runs the kit's
#      pinned shellcheck, bats lints and gofmt over the files the range changes (output on stderr); a failure
#      refuses. A push with no scripts/ci-local.sh in the work tree skips it, with a named stderr line.
#      (retro 2026-11-15 coordination-stretch C3)
#   5. Changelog gate (go/internal/changelog, the gate of scripts/changelog-gate.sh; CONTRIBUTING.md § 6.2).
#   6. Retro gate: a range that changes build-relevant kit files is BLOCKED unless it also carries a ledger
#      update (a ledger.d/ fragment or a BUILD-STATE.src.md edit) + a pending retro, OR a
#      `Retro: none (trivial: <reason>)` trailer, OR a `Retro: promotion (folds …)` trailer with a retro
#      header flipped pending -> folded or a ledger update. BUILD-STATE.md and retros/INDEX.md are GENERATED
#      and NOT committed, so the content half sweeps FRESH kit-state output in a temp dir: a malformed
#      fragment, source or retro header fails the push. A range that changes BUILD-STATE.src.md, ledger.d/
#      or retros/ runs that sweep at every exit, even the trivial one. [ev: retro ledger-generated-not-committed]
#      Retros and fragments are read from build-n4-module-kit/retros/ and build-n4-module-kit/ledger.d/ only (a
#      repository-level retros/ does not count); the refusal names both directories and the two ways out.
#      (retro 2026-11-15 coordination-stretch C6, T13)
# A git failure, an unreadable input or a missing tool refuses. So does this launcher: with no Go toolchain,
# a failed build or a missing go/ the push is refused, never let through unchecked.
#
# stdin (git pre-push contract): "<local ref> <local sha> <remote ref> <remote sha>" per ref; every line is gated.
set -u

refuse() { echo "pre-push: $1; refusing to push unchecked" >&2; exit 1; }

here="$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")")" && pwd)" || refuse "cannot resolve the hook directory"
GO_DIR="$here/../go"
[ -f "$GO_DIR/go-tool.sh" ] || refuse "no Go module at $GO_DIR (go-tool.sh missing), the gate cannot run"
# shellcheck disable=SC1091  # go/ helper, resolved at runtime via GO_DIR
. "$GO_DIR/go-tool.sh" || refuse "cannot load $GO_DIR/go-tool.sh"
GO_DIR="$(cd "$GO_DIR" && pwd)" || refuse "cannot enter $GO_DIR"
BIN="$(go_tool_bin "$GO_DIR" pre-push)" || refuse "the Go gate could not be built (above; install Go or fix the build)"
[ -x "$BIN" ] || refuse "the Go gate is not executable at ${BIN:-go/bin/pre-push}"
exec "$BIN" "$@"
